{
  "configuration_id": "config_010",
  "reason": "With only one completed experiment (config_001: rna_only, singleprofile, pca_n2000 → acc 0.485), evidence is extremely sparse and the most fundamental uncertainty is whether the image modality carries signal comparable to or stronger than RNA. Config_010 (image_only, singleprofile, resnet50) is a clean single-variable comparison against config_001: same profile setting (singleprofile), same simplicity (no aggregation, no fusion), differing only in modality/encoder. This isolates the question 'which modality is the stronger signal?' without confounding changes in profile setting, aggregation, or fusion. The answer is critical for all subsequent decisions: if image substantially outperforms RNA, we should prioritize image encoder and multimodal fusion experiments; if RNA is stronger, we focus on RNA encoder improvements; if both are weak, multimodal fusion becomes more appealing. No other single experiment reduces this top-level uncertainty as efficiently."
}

